/-!
# Zariski coverings of an algebraic space are detected on points

A *Zariski covering* of an algebraic space over a scheme `S`, in the sense of Stacks 02YY and
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsZariskiCover`, is a family of open subspaces whose coproduct
maps onto the space locally for the fppf topology. This file proves the part of Stacks 03BZ
which says that for a family of open subspaces that condition is equivalent to the much more
concrete one that the images of the point sets of the members cover the point set of the
space.

## Main definitions

No new definitions are introduced.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_ι_of_iUnion_range_pointsMap`: if the
  point sets of a family of open subspaces cover, the map from the coproduct of the members is
  locally surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.iUnion_range_pointsMap_of_isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_ι`: the
  converse.

The two together, **the Zariski-coverings part of Stacks 03BZ**, are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZariskiCover_iff_iUnion_points`, proved in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ZariskiCoveringPoints`.

## Implementation notes

**The two directions are proved by quite different arguments, and neither is the source's.**

*Point sets cover ⟹ locally surjective.* The sieve is produced explicitly rather than by
refining an abstract fppf covering. Fix a section `x` of the space over an object `T` of the
site, and let `ξ : h_T ⟶ F` be the morphism it names. Each member `X i` is an open subspace,
so its inclusion is relatively representable with open-immersion base changes: the pullback of
`X i` along `ξ` is an object `P i` of the site and `π i : P i ⟶ T` is an open immersion of
schemes. The family `π` is jointly surjective, because a point of `T` maps to a point of the
space, that point lies in some `X i` by hypothesis, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_points_of_isPullback` lifts the pair back to a point of
`P i`. A jointly surjective family of open immersions generates a covering sieve of the fppf
topology — `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_isOpenImmersion`, which is
the Zariski-coverings-are-fppf-coverings comparison — and over each `P i` the section `x`
restricts into `X i` by the very pullback square that produced `π i`, so it lifts to the
coproduct. No abstract refinement of a covering and no residue-field point is needed.

*Locally surjective ⟹ point sets cover.* The union `W` of the point sets is open, so part (1)
of Stacks 03BZ cuts out an open subspace `G` with `W` as its point set, and every member lies
below `G` by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.le_of_range_pointsMap_ι_subset`. The coproduct map
therefore factors through `G.ι`, so `G.ι` is itself locally surjective, hence an epimorphism
of fppf sheaves of types; it is a monomorphism because the inclusion of a subfunctor is; and
the category of sheaves of types is balanced. So `G.ι` is an isomorphism, its map on points is
surjective, and `W` is everything.

**The index type is in the working universe and that is not an accident.** `IsZariskiCover`
fixes `I : Type u`, and the coproduct `∐ fun i ↦ (X i).toFunctor` is taken in the presheaf
category `(BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u`, so the family has to be indexed there for the
coproduct to exist. The covering sieve produced in the first direction places no constraint of
its own: `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_isOpenImmersion` is stated at
an arbitrary index universe.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02YY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02YY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03BZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03BZ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### Point sets cover implies locally surjective -/

/-- **Half of the Zariski-coverings part of Stacks 03BZ.** If the point sets of a family of
open subspaces of an algebraic space over `S` cover its point set, then the map to the space
from the coproduct of the members is locally surjective for the fppf topology, which is the
covering condition of Stacks 02YY.

The covering sieve is generated by the base changes of the members along the section being
lifted; they are open immersions because the inclusion of an open subspace is a relatively
representable open immersion, and they are jointly surjective by the hypothesis together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_points_of_isPullback`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_ι_of_iUnion_range_pointsMap
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (I : Type u) (X : I → Subfunctor F)
    (hX : ∀ i, IsOpenSubspace B S hS (X i))
    (hcov : (⋃ i, Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (X i).toFunctor (X i).ι)) = Set.univ) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (X i).ι) := by
  constructor
  intro T x
  obtain ⟨ξ, rfl⟩ := yonedaEquiv.surjective x
  -- The base change of each member along the section.
  have hsq : ∀ i, IsPullback ((hX i).2.rep.fst ξ)
      (yoneda.map ((hX i).2.rep.snd ξ)) (X i).ι ξ := fun i ↦ (hX i).2.rep.isPullback ξ
  -- The base changes are jointly surjective on the points of the underlying scheme of `T`.
  have hjoint : ∀ t : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T,
      ∃ i, t ∈ Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((hX i).2.rep.snd ξ)) := by
    intro t
    obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ := surjective_pointsToScheme B S hS T t
    obtain ⟨i, a, ha⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp
      (hcov.ge (Set.mem_univ (pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj T) ξ τ)))
    obtain ⟨w, -, hw⟩ := exists_points_of_isPullback B S hS (hsq i) a τ ha
    refine ⟨i, pointsToScheme B S hS ((hX i).2.rep.pullback ξ) w, ?_⟩
    rw [← hτ, ← hw, pointsToScheme_pointsMap_yoneda]
  -- The generated sieve is covering, and refines the image sieve.
  refine (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).superset_covering ?_
    (BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS
      (fun i ↦ (hX i).2.rep.snd ξ) (fun i ↦ (hX i).2.property_snd ξ) hjoint)
  rintro Y g hg
  obtain ⟨i, a, rfl⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ g).mp hg
  refine ⟨(Sigma.ι (fun k ↦ (X k).toFunctor) i).app (Opposite.op Y)
    (yonedaEquiv (yoneda.map a ≫ (hX i).2.rep.fst ξ)), ?_⟩
  rw [← NatTrans.comp_app_apply, Sigma.ι_desc, ← yonedaEquiv_comp, Category.assoc, (hsq i).w,
    ← Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp, yonedaEquiv_naturality]

/-! ### Locally surjective implies point sets cover -/

/-- **The other half of the Zariski-coverings part of Stacks 03BZ.** If the map to an
algebraic space over `S` from the coproduct of a family of open subspaces is locally
surjective for the fppf topology, then the point sets of the members cover.

The union of the point sets is open, so part (1) of Stacks 03BZ realizes it as the point set of
an open subspace `G` which contains every member. The coproduct map factors through `G.ι`,
which is therefore locally surjective, hence epi among sheaves of types, and it is mono because
it is the inclusion of a subfunctor; sheaves of types are balanced, so it is an isomorphism. -/
theorem iUnion_range_pointsMap_of_isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_ι
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)
    (I : Type u) (X : I → Subfunctor F) (hX : ∀ i, IsOpenSubspace B S hS (X i))
    (hls : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (X i).ι)) :
    (⋃ i, Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (X i).toFunctor (X i).ι)) = Set.univ := by
  have _ : HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u) :=
    BigFppfOver.hasSheafify_type B S hS
  set G := openSubspaceOfPoints B S hS F
    (⋃ i, Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (X i).toFunctor (X i).ι))
  have hG : IsOpenSubspace B S hS G :=
    isOpenSubspace_openSubspaceOfPoints B S hS hF _ <| isOpen_iUnion fun i ↦
      isOpen_range_pointsMap_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS (X i).ι (hX i).2
  have hGrange : Set.range (pointsMap B S hS G.toFunctor G.ι) =
      ⋃ i, Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (X i).toFunctor (X i).ι) :=
    range_pointsMap_ι_openSubspaceOfPoints B S hS _
  have hle : ∀ i, X i ≤ G := fun i ↦
    le_of_range_pointsMap_ι_subset B S hS hG <| hGrange ▸
      Set.subset_iUnion (fun k ↦ Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (X k).toFunctor (X k).ι)) i
  -- The coproduct map factors through the inclusion of `G`.
  have hfac : (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ Subfunctor.homOfLe (hle i)) ≫ G.ι =
      Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (X i).ι := by
    refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, Sigma.ι_desc, Subfunctor.homOfLe_ι, Sigma.ι_desc]
  have hGls : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) G.ι :=
    Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac _ hfac
  -- `G.ι` is mono and epi among sheaves of types, hence an isomorphism.
  set φ : (⟨G.toFunctor, hG.1.isSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)) ⟶
      ⟨F, hF.isSheaf⟩ := ⟨G.ι⟩
  have _ : Epi φ := (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi φ).mp hGls
  have _ : Mono φ := (sheafToPresheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)).mono_of_mono_map
    (f := φ) (inferInstanceAs (Mono G.ι))
  have _ : IsIso φ := isIso_of_mono_of_epi φ
  have _ : IsIso G.ι := (sheafToPresheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)).map_isIso φ
  rw [← hGrange]
  exact (pointsMap_surjective_of_isIso B S hS G.ι).range_eq

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
